   "resumo_en": "The Five Faces of Manfred Mann is the debut British and second American studio album by Manfred Mann. It was first released in the United Kingdom on 11 September 1964 by His Master's Voice. In late October/early November, the album was released in Canada by Capitol Records. The Canadian track listing was almost the same as the UK version, except it included the hit \"Do Wah Diddy Diddy\" instead of \"I've Got My Mojo Working\". The record has been called \"one of the great blues-based British Invasion albums; it's a hot, rocking record that benefits from some virtuoso playing as well\".",
